  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ac6912242e2510442b83fca5c689cae7</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.14</version>
    <time>1787579029</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.4.14, and stop guessing a GPU vendor

Supersedes request 1373165, adding one patch on top of the same 0.4.14
update.

detect_vendor() looked for &quot;+cu&quot; or &quot;+rocm&quot; in the PyTorch version
string. Only upstream's own wheels carry that suffix, so a distribution
PyTorch never matched and init() then logged

  Could not autodetect AIMDO implementation, assuming Nvidia

on every ComfyUI start, for every user, whatever hardware they have. It
now reads the cuda and hip attributes that the same version module
already defines, and when PyTorch has neither it reports failure with an
informational message instead of naming a vendor it never selected. That
path is what happens here regardless, since the native allocator is not
built.

%check now exercises it. Local build green on both flavours, rpmlint clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1373273</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>5e242670359eff88058c886564a46d63</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.15</version>
    <time>1787766808</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-comfy-aimdo to 0.4.15.

The entire upstream 0.4.14..0.4.15 delta is a single Windows-only
constant: NVML_BUDGET_HEADROOM in src-win/shmem-detect.c drops from
768 MB to 512 MB. The comfy_aimdo Python tree that this package ships
is byte-identical to 0.4.14, so there is no functional change for
openSUSE users.

Upstream publishes no sdist on PyPI, so the source stays the GitHub tag
tarball; its sha256 was checked against a freshly fetched copy of the
tag. Patch0 is retained unchanged and still applies cleanly, as the
upstream pull request behind it has not been merged.

Built and verified on aarch64: rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 badness,
and %check passes for python313 and python314.

Staging note: Factory's comfyui pinned this package to an exact version,
which would have gone unresolvable when this landed. Request 1373685
converts that pin to a floor (and fixes a second, already-broken exact
pin on comfyui-workflow-templates). Please stage the two together, or
let 1373685 land first.</comment>
    <requestid>1373687</requestid>
  </revision>
